<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  ============================================================
  cr-dotnet-0010 FIX: Web.config Transformation Eliminated
  ============================================================
  This Web.Release.config transformation file has been superseded
  by runtime environment variable injection and AWS Systems Manager
  (SSM) Parameter Store as part of the cloud-readiness remediation
  for rule cr-dotnet-0010 (Web.config Transformations).

  RATIONALE:
  Build-time Web.config transformations bake environment-specific
  configuration into deployment artifacts, preventing immutable
  deployments and true infrastructure-as-code practices. In a
  cloud-native AWS deployment, all environment-specific settings
  are injected at runtime via:

    1. Environment Variables (ECS task definitions, Elastic Beanstalk
       environment properties, Lambda environment config, etc.)
    2. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store (SSM) for structured
       configuration and secrets management.
    3. AWS Secrets Manager for sensitive credentials (DB passwords,
       API keys, etc.).

  MIGRATION GUIDE — Release-environment settings previously managed
  here should now be configured as follows:

  CONNECTION STRINGS:
    Previously: Web.config <connectionStrings> transformed per environment
    Now:        Set the environment variable RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING
                at runtime (e.g., in ECS task definition environment block
                or Elastic Beanstalk environment properties).
                Example (production):
                  RDS_PROXY_CONNECTION_STRING=Server=<rds-proxy-endpoint>;
                    Database=DBProject;User Id=<user>;Password=<from-secrets-manager>

  DEBUG / COMPILATION FLAGS:
    Previously: <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" />
                (removed the debug="true" attribute for release builds)
    Now:        Set ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production (or ASP.NET_ENV for
                classic ASP.NET) in the runtime environment. The application
                reads this variable to disable debug-level logging and
                detailed error pages automatically.

  APPLICATION SETTINGS:
    Previously: <appSettings> keys transformed per environment
    Now:        Store in AWS SSM Parameter Store under a path such as
                /HospitalMgmt/Production/<KeyName> and retrieve at startup
                using the AWS SDK (AWSSDK.SimpleSystemsManagement NuGet
                package) or the AWS AppConfig integration.

  CUSTOM ERRORS:
    Previously: <customErrors mode="RemoteOnly" xdt:Transform="Replace" />
    Now:        Configure error handling middleware in the application code
                based on the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT / ASP.NET_ENV variable.
                In production, detailed errors are suppressed automatically.

  SECRETS MANAGEMENT:
    Database passwords, API keys, and other secrets must be stored in
    AWS Secrets Manager and retrieved at runtime. Never store secrets
    in Web.config, environment variable files committed to source control,
    or build artifacts.

  This file is intentionally left without active XDT transformation
  directives. It is retained in the project only for reference and
  to satisfy MSBuild project file references. It performs no
  build-time transformation.
  ============================================================
-->

<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No build-time transformations are applied in this file.
    All environment-specific configuration is supplied at runtime
    via environment variables and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store.
    See the migration guide in the comment block above.
  -->
</configuration>
